 "level": "A2",
 "blurb": "English for Daily Life takes an adult beginner who already knows a little English and gives them the present and the past: what is, what they do, and what happened. Eight units follow six people who live at one address, so the vocabulary comes back week after week instead of arriving once and leaving. Every unit has the same ten parts, the same twelve kinds of exercise and the same support: a worked example at the top of almost every task, a model before every piece of writing, a word bank under every gap-fill and a checklist before you hand anything in. The Core track is for everybody. The Plus track at the back of each unit is there when you are ready for it, and optional when you are not. Answers for every closed question are in the book.",
 "units": [
  "People and Routines",
  "Home and Neighbourhood",
